[{:adr/related ["2607100100-runtime-priority-apps-jvm-bb-demoted" "2607124500-bmc-business-operate-daily-product-completeness-and-nbb-fix" "2607181900-kbb-kotoba-script-host-priority"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607173000", :adr/context "Superproject tooling already on nbb (PR #336) but ~134 child bb.edn and ~86 *.bb scripts remained. Owner request 2026-07-17: Babashka を全て nbb に.", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/helpers ["scripts/nbb-run-tests.cljs" "scripts/verify-no-babashka.cljs" "scripts/bb-to-nbb-scaffold.cljs"], :adr/exit-criteria "{:bb.edn-count 0, :dot-bb-count 0, :superproject-bb-invocations 0}", :adr/body "# ADR-2607173000: Fleet-wide Babashka → nbb (bb binary retirement)\n\n**Status**: accepted  \n**Date**: 2026-07-17  \n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner request「Babashka を全て nbb に」)  \n**Related**: ADR-2607100100 (runtime priority; superproject tooling nbb port addendum),\nPR #336 (`chore(tooling): migrate root babashka/shell tooling to nbb`),\nADR-2607124500 (BMC routine bb→nbb command fix)\n\n## Context\n\nSuperproject operational tooling (`scripts/`, `manifest/`, `70-tools/bmc/`,\n`.claude/hooks/`) already runs on **nbb** (PR #336 / ADR-2607100100 addendum).\n`scripts/nbb_compat` provides Node stand-ins for historical `babashka.*` /\n`clojure.java.*` APIs so ported scripts keep compiling.\n\nThat port left a **fleet gap**:\n\n| Surface | ~Count (2026-07-17) |\n|---------|---------------------|\n| Child `bb.edn` | ~134 |\n| Child `*.bb` scripts | ~86 (edn-datomize / publish / gen-shadow families) |\n| Child `nbb.edn` | 2 only |\n| Superproject residual `bb` invocations | scripts/hooks/skills/workflows |\n\nADR-2607100100 Decision §3 deferred full ops tooling migration to a separate\nADR. This ADR **closes that deferral** for the entire west-managed fleet:\n**no workflow, script, CI job, or agent instruction should require the `bb`\nbinary.**\n\nnbb is not SCI-identical (no raw Java interop, no babashka pods, explicit\nclasspath). JVM remains a last-resort **app** runtime for work that truly\nneeds it (`clojure -M:…`, Playwright Java, etc.). This program retires **bb\nas the task/script host**, not JVM application code.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Canonical scripting / task host = nbb only** across the superproject and\n   every west project under `orgs/`.\n2. **`bb.edn` and `#!/usr/bin/env bb` are forbidden** in new work and must be\n   removed in waves (below). Scaffolds emit `nbb.edn` + package.json / nbb\n   test entry — never `bb.edn`.\n3. **`scripts/nbb_compat` may keep `babashka.*` namespace names** as temporary\n   shims so existing nbb scripts need not rename requires in the same PR.\n   Shim namespaces are not a license to invoke the `bb` binary.\n4. **Task registry**: babashka `:tasks` has no nbb equivalent. Prefer:\n   - `nbb.edn` for `:paths`\n   - `nbb <script>.cljs` / `nbb -m <ns>` / shared `scripts/nbb-run-tests.cljs`\n   - `package.json` scripts for multi-command surfaces\n   - `clojure -M:…` / `npx …` only when the work itself requires JVM or Node\n     tools — orchestrated without bb\n5. **Wave plan** (land separately; do not force-push):\n\n| Wave | Scope |\n|------|--------|\n| 0 | Superproject residual + ADR + `nbb-run-tests` + `verify-no-babashka` + CLAUDE.md |\n| 1 | Shared script families: publish, edn-datomize fan-out, gen-shadow-cljs-edn |\n| 2 | Mechanical scaffold `bb.edn` (~88–100 repos): sci-test + shell-only patterns |\n| 3 | Large custom `bb.edn` (cloud-itonami, network-isekai, local-manimani, murakumo, etzhayyim/root, …) |\n| 4 | Enforcement sweep; new-project-scaffold skill; final inventory → 0 |\n\n6. **Historical ADR prose** is not mass-rewritten (lesson from closed PR #442).\n   Live call sites (README, CLAUDE, skills, CI, scripts) are updated.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Agents and humans use `nbb …` exclusively for repo scripts.\n- Child repos gain `nbb.edn` where classpath is needed; delete `bb.edn` after\n  the replacement test path is verified.\n- Pin advances land per-repo (or small batches) via existing west/fleet rules.\n- Optional CI/agent gate: `nbb scripts/verify-no-babashka.cljs` fails on new\n  `bb.edn` / `#!/usr/bin/env bb` under tracked paths.\n\n## Exit criteria\n\n- [ ] `fd -t f 'bb.edn' orgs` → 0\n- [ ] `fd -t f '\\.bb$' orgs` → 0\n- [ ] Superproject live paths: no `bb` command invocation\n- [ ] Scaffold skill emits nbb-only tooling\n- [ ] This ADR addendum records final inventory\n\n## Wave 0 landing (this commit series)\n\n- Policy ADR (this document + edn pair)\n- CLAUDE.md: ops tooling is nbb-only (closes “bb が正本” wording)\n- Residual: `migrate-etzhayyim-compat`, kami-webgpu audit test discovery,\n  design-quality workflow/skill call sites\n- Shared helpers: `scripts/nbb-run-tests.cljs`, `scripts/verify-no-babashka.cljs`,\n  `scripts/bb_to_nbb_scaffold.cljs` (classifier + emitter for Wave 2),\n  `scripts/gen-shadow-cljs-edn.cljs` (Wave 1 shared template)\n\n## Progress (2026-07-17)\n\n| Wave | Status |\n|------|--------|\n| 0 Superproject residual + helpers | **done** (merged to main) |\n| 1 Shared `.bb` families | partial — `gen-shadow-cljs-edn.cljs` in superproject; publish/edn-datomize fan-out still open |\n| 2 Scaffold `bb.edn` | **~45** `kotoba-lang/com-*` sci-test repos landed (emit + `npm test` green + server merge). More sci-test / shell-only remaining outside that set |\n| 3 Large custom `bb.edn` | open (cloud-itonami, network-isekai, local-manimani, murakumo, etzhayyim/root, …) |\n| 4 Enforcement | open |\n\n**Follow-up required:** west pin advance for every landed child repo (child `main`\nhas the nbb files; superproject pins still point at pre-migration SHAs until\n`gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry <name>` / fleet pin-advance).\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-17 continued)\n\n- Wave 2 pin advance: ~45 `kotoba-lang/com-*` pins verified and written to west.yml.\n- Wave 3: `cloud-itonami` bb.edn → `scripts/tasks.edn` + `run-task.cljs` (164 shellable tasks) landed on main.\n- Wave 3 batch: ~25 additional project-root bb.edn converted+merged; remaining project-root bb.edn ≈ worktree/fork/etzhayyim-root only.\n- Helper: `scripts/bb_edn_to_nbb_tasks.cljs` for large bb.edn conversion.\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-17 — next wave)\n\n- Clean-base re-land of conflicted remotes: freeboard, murakumo, kami-webgpu, kami-genko, io-multiformats, org-chainagnostic-cacao, org-ietf-turn, kawaraban, …\n- `edn-datomize.bb` fan-out: ~19 child repos → standalone nbb `edn-datomize.cljs` (schema at repo-root `schema.edn`)\n- `publish.bb` runtime: `com-junkawasaki/kototama` + `kotoba-lang/kototama` → `publish.cljs`\n- `etzhayyim/root` bb.edn retired on main (3 shellable + 95 complex catalogued in tasks-complex.edn)\n- Project-root `bb.edn` remaining: worktree/fork only (`_wt-pr427`, `cloud-itonami-current`)\n- Helpers: `scripts/edn_datomize_standalone.cljs`, `scripts/publish_actor_standalone.cljs`\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-17 — final fan-out)\n\n- Nested `edn-datomize.bb` under `etzhayyim/root/20-actors/*` → nbb (14 files)\n- Remaining standalone edn-datomize for subaru/sanae\n- All 10 etzhayyim actor `methods/publish.cljs` wrappers on main\n- `etzhayyim/root`: 54 require/-main tasks promoted to `nbb -m` / nbb -e; 41 remain in tasks-complex (python shells, multi-require test suites, etc.)\n- Helper: `scripts/wire_tasks_complex.cljs`\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-20 — Wave 2 continuation)\n\n- Local `orgs/kotoba-lang` snapshot: 900 bb.edn total (832 `:sci-test`-class,\n  17 `:shell-only`, 51 `:complex`; the 51 complex are almost entirely\n  non-`com-*` repos — webgpu-*/murakumo/kami-*/freeboard/org-*). Fleet-wide\n  (all orgs) local snapshot: 1095 bb.edn, 826 under `kotoba-lang/com-*`.\n- New pipeline: fresh `--depth 1` clone to scratch (not the shared/stale\n  `orgs/` checkout, which was found dirty + detached HEAD + several commits\n  behind for sampled repos) → `scripts/bb_to_nbb_scaffold.cljs emit` →\n  `npm test` gate → branch → push → `gh api .../merges` server-side merge →\n  remote branch delete. Script: scratchpad `bb-to-nbb-batch.sh` (session-local,\n  not committed).\n- This session landed 60 additional `kotoba-lang/com-*` sci-test conversions\n  (com-flipkart, com-ietf-rfcs, com-airtable, com-neurable, com-biconomy,\n  com-amtrak, com-palantir-gotham, com-kustomer, com-maxar-technologies,\n  com-mckesson, com-apigee, com-nhtsa, com-doordash, com-jpo-patents,\n  com-samsara, com-gong, com-fca-uk, com-boj, com-paystack,\n  com-quintessencelabs, com-procore-construction, com-goodrx, com-noaa,\n  com-materials-project, com-nvidia-nvml, com-amadeus-altea,\n  com-fix-fast-protocol, com-hologram, com-fawry, com-paycom,\n  com-apple-visionos, com-firebase, com-iceye, com-openbankinguk,\n  com-relayhealth, com-ge-proficy, com-enverus, com-fbi-ucr, com-camel-ai,\n  com-ncts, com-particle, com-citi-velocity, com-onnx-runtime,\n  com-outsystems, com-d-wave, com-freja-eid, com-netsuite,\n  com-bloomberg-law, com-metagraph, com-munich-re-api, com-ge-aviation,\n  com-fmcg-traceability, com-canvaslms, com-replicate, com-isic-codes,\n  com-digitalocean, com-b-pipe, com-matillion, com-cesium-xr, com-dtcc) —\n  30/30 then 29/30 landed (1 skip: com-flexport already migrated upstream,\n  stale local pin). All merged to each child repo's `main` directly via\n  server-side merge; 0 test failures.\n- **Discovered incidentally**: several repos (com-8th-wall,\n  com-eclinicalworks, com-flexport) already have `nbb.edn` on upstream\n  `main` with no `bb.edn` — the local `orgs/kotoba-lang` snapshot undercounts\n  true remaining work because local checkouts are stale/pin-behind, not\n  because those conversions are outstanding. A `west update` + fresh\n  `classify` pass (or GitHub-API-based classify) would give an accurate\n  remaining count instead of the local-filesystem snapshot used here.\n- **Not yet done this session**: west pin advance for any of the 60 landed\n  repos (child `main` has nbb.edn; superproject `manifest/west.yml` pins\n  still point at pre-migration SHAs — same follow-up gap noted in the\n  2026-07-17 addenda above, now larger). Remaining local `kotoba-lang/com-*`\n  sci-test backlog after this batch: ≈765 (826 − 60 landed − 1 discovered\n  already-done, before accounting for further stale-pin overcounting).\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-20 — Wave 2 batch 3)\n\n- Third batch of 30 `kotoba-lang/com-*` repos processed with the same fresh-clone -> scaffold-emit -> npm-test-gate -> server-merge pipeline: 28 landed, 2 discovered already migrated upstream (com-bgp-routing, com-autodesk — stale local pins again, not real remaining work). 0 test failures.\n- Session cumulative: 87 `kotoba-lang/com-*` repos landed (batch1 30 + batch2 29 + batch3 28, minus overlap/manual com-flipkart counted once), 5 more discovered already-done upstream via stale local pins (com-8th-wall, com-eclinicalworks, com-flexport, com-bgp-routing, com-autodesk).\n- West pin advance for all landed repos is still outstanding (same gap as the previous addendum).\n\n## Progress addendum (2026-07-20 — Wave 2 batch 4)\n\n- Fourth batch of 30 `kotoba-lang/com-*` repos: 27 landed, 3 discovered already migrated upstream (com-kajabi, com-shodan, com-airbus-analytx — stale local pins again). 0 test failures.\n- Session cumulative: 114 `kotoba-lang/com-*` repos landed (batch1 30 + batch2 29 + batch3 28 + batch4 27), 9 more discovered already-done upstream via stale local pins.\n- West pin advance for all landed repos is still outstanding (unchanged gap).\n\n## Addendum (2026-07-18 — forward priority, does not change this ADR's decision)\n\nADR-2607181900 sets a **future** script/tooling-host priority of `kbb`\n（Kotoba script host, not yet implemented）→ `nbb` → (retired: `bb`), extending\nthe app/library runtime order (ADR-2607100100) into the ops-tooling track\nthis ADR carved out. It explicitly does not flip this ADR's decision: `nbb`\nremains the canonical script/task host, the bb-retirement waves and\n`verify-no-babashka.cljs` gate above are unchanged, and no script should\nassume `kbb` exists until ADR-2607181900's readiness gate is met.", :adr/decision "{:script-host :nbb-only, :forbid [\"bb.edn\" \"#!/usr/bin/env bb\" \"bb binary in live call sites\"], :allow-shim-namespaces [\"babashka.fs\" \"babashka.process\" \"babashka.curl\"], :task-registry [:nbb.edn :package.json :nbb-run-tests :nbb-m], :waves {0 :superproject-residual+helpers, 1 :shared-script-families, 2 :scaffold-bb.edn-bulk, 3 :large-custom-bb.edn, 4 :enforcement+inventory}, :no-historical-adr-mass-rewrite true}", :adr/date "2026-07-17", :db/id -1, :adr/title "Fleet-wide Babashka → nbb (bb binary retirement)", :adr/source-format "edn"}]